# Dev-branch-only artifacts (tracked on main-full-dev, never on main).
# Anchored to the repo root so they can never shadow source paths;
# On main and any branch cut from main these paths do not exist, so
# a plain git-add-dot can never pick them up; on main-full-dev they are
# tracked, and tracked files are unaffected by ignore rules.
/.agents/
/.superdesign/
/aics/
/docs/
/graphify-out/
/scripts/
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
/CONTEXT.md
/TODO.md
/skills-lock.json

# Sandbox/dev-environment only folders (never ship, never track).
# Anchored to the repo root so they can never shadow source paths
# (the old unanchored `aics/` rule also matched src/lib/aics and
# made `git add` refuse tracked source files).
/.zscripts/
/db/
/download/
/mini-services/
/prisma/
/tests/
/tool-results/
/upload/
/agent-ctx/
/skills/
/worklog.md

# Agent config
.z-ai-config
package-lock.json
